# comments
# comment 0011a050 camp menu root update (21 states, jpt 0x7B5420): loads the camp PAKs, opens H_CampRootDraw, then one sub-screen per selection (0 Skill 0x1617D0, 1 Item 0x14EE80, 2 Persona 0x1336B0, 3 Equip 0x130F20, 4 Status 0x123570, 5 S.Link 0x136750, 6 System 0x1548A0), waiting for kwlnTaskGetState == 3; returns -1 when closed
# comment 0011b420 camp main list (11 states): state 6 reads the pad (0x20 cancel -> selection -2, 0x40 confirm -> selection = cursor; up/down 0x4000/0x1000 with wrap, index 5 skipped in The Answer); highlight y = 59 + 19 * cursor at gp-0x4DA4 + 0x320
# comment 0011abd0 H_Camp_MoveListCursor(count, page, &scroll, &cursor): list navigation shared by the sub-screens; up/down/page with wrap-around, one SFX per move, writes the two out-params only when moved
# comment 0016ef20 the s16 game date at 0x83679C: days since April 5 (0 = 4/5, a Sunday)
# comment 0016f190 datGetFlag(id): bit id % 32 of u32 word id / 32 at 0x83A21C (gGlobalWork + 0x401C, 176 words = 5632 flags), C truncating division
# comment 0017d830 month of a day count: rem = (s16)(days + 4); month = 4; while (rem >= len[month-1]) { rem -= len; month = month == 12 ? 1 : month + 1 } (len = s16[12] at 0x5E3B60)
# comment 0017d8b0 days since April 5 of (month, day): sum of len[4-1].. up to month (month counted down to 4, 0 wraps to 12) + day - 5; May 1 = 26, Jan 1 = 271
# comment 0017dae0 weekday = (days + 7) % 7 through div/mfhi; 0 = Sunday
# comment 00181b50 moon phase byte of day n from the 368-byte table at 0x5E38D0; 0x0E = full moon (first on day 4 = 4/9)
# comment 00183410 H_DayPartsDraw update (9 states, jpt 0x7B6600): loads camp/i_moon_00.spr, draws the date/weekday/day-part HUD via sub_1842C0 every frame, runs the day/time change animations (H_DayChgDraw / H_TimeChgDraw children) when the date or part changes
# comment 001842c0 draws the date HUD: panel 0x3A, time band 0x39 (green tint when part == 8), month/day digits, weekday glyph, day-part name with fade, and "Next N" = days to the next 0x0E in the moon table (sprites 0x4C, 0x23 + digit) unless flag 0x1420
# comment 001005b0 H_Cursor_CreateTask(parent, {x,y} in a1, rect[4] in a2, rgba in a3, z in f12): 0x150-byte work, task "H CURSOR Draw" prio 0x18BF; the update rebuilds four Im2D vertices from pos/rect(w,h as ints)/z/colour and draws a tri-strip
# comment 00112110 .SPR loader states: 0 H_Cdvd_Request, 1 32-byte header -> +0x198 (+0x1AC textures, +0x1AE sprites), 2 per texture {u32, u32 offset} -> uttmxCreateRaster -> +0x104[i], 4 per sprite {u32, u32 offset} -> 0x80-byte records at +0x184, 5 ready
# comment 003afad0 frAddFontStyle(style, fnt, cdvd): style record 32 B at 0x95ACF0 + 32*style = {owner, fnt, size1, size2, widths, block2, glyph block, Huffman block}; FNT: +0xA CLUT blocks*64, +0xE glyph count, +0x10/+0x12 w/h, +0x14 bytes/glyph, +0x16 tables flag; widths = s8[count][2] {left, right}
# comment 003b0620 glyph index: c < 0x80 ? (c == 0x20 ? 0x1F7 : c - 0x20) : (((c - 0x8080) & 0xFF00) >> 1) + ((c - 0x8080) & 0x7F); >= count -> 0x147; creates a 0x2C-byte glyph node from ring buffer 1
# comment 003b47b0 fmGslDecodeGlyph(dst, glyph, hdr, regions): Huffman decode of bits offsets[glyph]..offsets[glyph+1] from the u16 stream (LSB first, 17-bit shift register) through 6-byte nodes {u16, child0, child1} (leaf when child0 == 0, symbol at +4); one byte per leaf, 512 for a 32x32 4-bpp glyph
# comment 003b4770 fmGslGetGlyphBlocks(hdr, out[3]): dictionary = hdr + hdr[0], offsets = dictionary + hdr[1], stream = offsets + hdr[6]
# comment 003a8170 message window frame: sprites 0x12 (x 225) and 0x13 (x 561) of facility/i_mes_win01.spr at a y from the line count, through itfMesManagerDrawSpriteEx
# comment 00192b50 The Journey / The Answer choice: up/down toggles +4, confirm (gPadFlags & 0x40) creates HonpenFileSetup (datSetScenarioMode 0) or GojitudanFileSetup (1); drawn with H_Dbprt_FmtAt
# comment 00193020 carry-over ("hikitsugi") flow of a new game: four buffers (0x50, 0x3400, 0x2C0, 0x2C), Y_Misc_CreateMcTasks, applies the loaded data with sub_192E70
# comment 00188690 boot-time memory card check: mcWNDProc tasks, message ids 0xF / 0x10 / 0x15, H_Memcard_UpdateChkAreaSeq result 0x64 = done
# comment 0027de40 loads the eight battle .TBL records of 0x692D40 (SKILL, UNIT, MSG, PERSONA, ENCOUNT, EFFECT, MODEL, AICALC; _F variants) through sub_27DCD0; a0 != 0 loads all synchronously, else one per call
# comment 0016c2f0 slices event/itemtbl.bin at 0x83BB30 into 14 section pointers (gp-0x4D0C..-0x4D38) from the count words and a 35-entry 32-byte table at 0x83AAA0
